Hello d-i porters,

Now that 2.6.16-15 kernels have been uploaded to unstable (using a=20
linux-2.6.16 source package), we can start thinking about the Etch Beta 3=20
release of D-I.

Currently all architectures, except for arm, have built 2.6.16-15 and it=20
should be available from the mirrors tomorrow.

Please rebuild and upload your kernel udeb packages against these new=20
kernel images as soon as possible. Note that there have been some recent=20
changes in kernel-wedge which may affect your builds.

Note also that 2.6.17 has been uploaded to unstable as well (currently in=20
NEW). Do _not_ build the kernel udebs against that, but against 2.6.16!

If you have a chance to run some tests using daily images after the new=20
kernel udebs have been uploaded, that would be very much appreciated.

I will post a more detailed release plan as soon as it is clear when the=20
2.6.16 kernel packages will migrate to testing. Some information about=20
Beta 3 is already available from [1].

If there are any issues for your architecture that we should be aware of,=20
please let us know.

Cheers,
=46JP

[1] http://wiki.debian.org/DebianInstaller/EtchBeta3Prep

